---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import {paidProduct,supportEmail} from '../lib/paid-product.mjs';
---
<Base title="Deal Lab paid-beta pricing" description="A purpose-built acquisition-learning workspace: $19 per month or $190 per year. The core course remains free." type="About" noindex>
 <article class="narrow" data-paid-page>
  <header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">Paid beta</p><h1>Analyze the assumptions before you risk your capital.</h1><p>A purpose-built AI workspace for interactive acquisition analysis and practice.</p><p class="small spaced">The initial paid beta is invite-only for customers in the United States. <span data-pricing-beta-request>Contact <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a> to request Checkout approval.</span> The core course remains free and globally accessible.</p></header>
  <p class="notice" data-paid-status role="status" aria-live="polite">Checking Deal Lab availability…</p>
  <fieldset class="spaced" data-checkout-attestation hidden><legend>Paid-beta eligibility</legend><label><input type="checkbox" data-us-attestation/> I confirm that I am a U.S. customer and understand that this initial paid beta is available only to U.S. customers.</label></fieldset>
  <section class="section" style="border-top:0"><h2>{paidProduct.name}</h2><div class="plans spaced"><div><h3>${paidProduct.monthlyUsd}<span class="small"> / month</span></h3><p>Monthly subscription</p><button class="button spaced" data-checkout="monthly" hidden>Choose monthly</button></div><div><h3>${paidProduct.annualUsd}<span class="small"> / year</span></h3><p>Annual subscription</p><button class="button spaced" data-checkout="annual" hidden>Choose annual</button></div></div><p class="small muted spaced">Includes up to {paidProduct.monthlyRequestAllowance} AI requests per UTC month, on either billing interval. Renews monthly or annually until canceled. No free AI trial. Requests that reach the model count even if a response fails; access-denied and quota-denied attempts do not count.</p><p class="small spaced">The course, topics, examples and source-linked educational material remain free. Deal Lab subscriptions support interactive AI analysis, deterministic calculations, deal-reasoning workflows, fictional deal practice and IC workflows, and associated model and compute costs.</p><p class="small spaced"><a href="/account/" data-account-link>Already subscribed? Sign in</a></p></section>
  <section class="section prose"><h2>Practice the decisions that connect a deal.</h2><ul><li>Use interactive AI analysis to examine valuation and add-backs against the evidence supplied.</li><li>Connect financing and debt capacity, then model debt service, DSCR and downside sensitivities with deterministic calculations.</li><li>Reason through diligence, working capital, offer terms and deal structure.</li><li>Review curriculum-grounded sources alongside an answer.</li><li>Practice with fictional Deal Lab cases, carry deal reasoning across turns, and defend an acquisition thesis in IC Challenge.</li></ul><p>The AI helps you examine evidence and assumptions. You retain responsibility for decisions; an answer does not establish lender approval or replace transaction-specific professional advice.</p></section>
  <section class="section prose"><h2>Why not just use ChatGPT?</h2><p>You absolutely can use a general AI assistant. Acquisition Companion is designed for buyers who don’t want to build their own M&amp;A prompts, models and learning framework from scratch.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Different ways to organize the learning work</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Build your own workflow</th><th scope="col">Acquisition Companion</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Choose questions, prompts and a learning sequence.</td><td>A curriculum and acquisition-specific practice modes.</td></tr><tr><td>Supply and evaluate the sources you want to use.</td><td>Linked curriculum sources with explicit provenance.</td></tr><tr><td>Design and check the calculation approach.</td><td>Deterministic deal calculations with stated inputs and assumptions.</td></tr><tr><td>Organize valuation, financing, downside, diligence and structure.</td><td>A workflow connecting those questions, plus investment-committee practice.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="small spaced">The distinction is workflow, sources, calculations, curriculum and guardrails. We do not claim a superior underlying AI model or exclusive analytical capabilities.</p></section>
  <p class="small spaced">Need help with sign-in, subscriptions or cancellations? <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>. <a href="/terms/">Review the billing terms</a>.</p>
  <section class="section prose"><h2>The course stands on its own.</h2><p>The free lessons, worked examples and reference libraries are useful without AI or an account. <a href="/course/">Follow the course</a>, <a href="/examples/">work through the examples</a>, or <a href="/methodology/">inspect the methodology</a>. AI Deal Lab is the application layer for practice.</p><p>Practice with fictional or public information. Do not submit confidential, proprietary, personal or non-public deal material. No private CIM or document uploads. <a href="/privacy/">Read the current privacy policy.</a></p><div class="actions spaced"><a href="/ai/">Open AI Deal Lab →</a></div></section>
 </article>
 <script src="../scripts/paid-account.ts"></script>
</Base>

<style>.plans{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:2rem}.plans h3{font-size:2rem}@media(max-width:520px){.plans{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:1.5rem}}</style>
